  "details": "1. Report ~100 avatars (legitimately) in 2-4 hours to hit an API rate limit (lasts for ~4 hours).\n\n2. Try to report something, get the rate limited error message: Error submitting report: \"whatever it is that you are doing, you are doing it too quickly. slow down!\"\n\n3. Try to click on \"Learn More\" and see it doesn't actually have any help topic on this error and takes to the generic help page index.\n\nExpected result: I don't know, take the user to a help page about errors / rate limiting when \"Learn More\" is pressed?\n\nActual result: The help page index is shown when \"Learn More\" is pressed about this error.\n\nAdditional info: Video, and the relevant logs:\n\n```\n\n2026.07.16 22:11:09 Error      -  [API] [1184, 429, Post, -1 https://api.vrchat.cloud/api/1/moderationReports] Abandoning request, because - \"whatever it is that you are doing, you are doing it too quickly. slow down!\"\n\n2026.07.16 22:11:09 Error      -  Error submitting report: \"whatever it is that you are doing, you are doing it too quickly. slow down!\"\n\n```",
